# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.
# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.
#
# LOCAL DEV ON WINDOWS — PREFER THE CREDENTIAL MANAGER, NOT THIS FILE.
# A key in .env is plaintext at rest and readable by every process running as you (including
# anything you npm install). Store it under DPAPI instead and load it with the gitignored
# wrapper in scripts/local/:
#     cmdkey /generic:JanusGeminiApiKey /user:gemini /pass:<your AI Studio key>
#     node scripts/local/with-secrets.mjs npm run verify:live-voice
# Setup, rationale, and the fail-closed contract: docs/process/LOCAL_SECRETS.md
# (The server itself never persists this key — there is no geminiApiKey field in
# .janus_settings.json — so a .env would be weaker than what the running system already does.)
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.
# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"
